  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "What to Ask Before Hiring a Contractor for a Bathroom Addition",
    "text": "What to Ask Before Hiring a Contractor for a Bathroom Addition",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Planning a brand-new bathroom addition comes with big structural and plumbing questions. Before signing any contract, you need to know how the space will function and who is handling each phase of construction.\n\nWhat to Ask Before You Decide\nFirst, ask how your current plumbing layout impacts the budget. Connecting to distant sewer stacks or opening concrete slabs adds complexity, so you want to know if existing water and drain lines can realistically support new fixtures. Second, clarify permit handling and inspection scheduling. A legal addition requires plumbing, electrical, and structural approvals to ensure safety and code compliance. Third, ask who manages the day-to-day work. Working with a hands-on general contractor who leads framing and tile work while coordinating licensed sub-trades for mechanicals prevents miscommunication and costly delays. Finally, verify how waterproofing and outside-vented exhaust fans are handled to protect your home from long-term moisture issues.\n\nWhen you are ready to evaluate your layout and review your project scope in the greater Denver area, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your plans.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
